---
import BlogPostLayout from '../../../../layouts/BlogPostLayout.astro';

const title = "Government psychologist salary in India per month: what each post pays";
const description = "Government psychologist salary in India per month runs from Rs 25,000 on entry contract posts to about Rs 91,000 (basic plus DA) at Level 10. See each post.";
const canonical = "https://futurecareerschool.com/blog/government-jobs/government-psychologist-salary-india-per-month/";
const publishedDateISO = "2026-11-15";
const publishedDateLabel = "15 November 2026";
const authorName = 'Shivanshi Sehgal';
const authorUrl = 'https://futurecareerschool.com/about/shivanshi-sehgal/';
const authorRole = 'Career researcher and writer';

const faqItems = [
  {
    q: "How much does a government psychologist earn per month in India?",
    a: "In the notices checked between 2022 and 2026, contract clinical psychologist posts paid Rs 25,000 to Rs 50,000 a month, and a faculty-level contract paid Rs 1,30,000. Level 10 posts such as DRDO Scientist 'B' (Psychology) and AIIMS clinical posts start at Rs 56,100 basic pay, which is about Rs 91,000 a month with 63% dearness allowance, before house rent allowance and deductions."
  },
  {
    q: "Is a government psychologist's salary fixed?",
    a: "A regular post follows a pay level, and dearness allowance is revised by the government. A contract post usually pays one fixed amount, and the contract is renewed on a set term, such as 179 days at first or one year at a time. Read the pay line of the notice before you compare two posts."
  },
  {
    q: "Do I need RCI registration for a government psychologist job?",
    a: "For clinical psychologist posts, yes in most notices. The Kerala PSC notice asked for an M.Phil in Clinical Psychology or a two-year equivalent from an RCI-approved institute, plus RCI registration. Counsellor posts can differ: the Delhi Tele MANAS notice accepted a master's degree in psychology or social work for its counsellor post."
  },
  {
    q: "Which government psychologist post pays the most?",
    a: "Among the notices checked, a faculty-level contract at the NIMHANS Tele MANAS centre paid Rs 1,30,000 consolidated, and it asked for a PhD in Clinical Psychology plus three years of teaching or research. Among regular posts, Level 10 is where the notices checked started. Pay moves up with experience and promotion rules."
  },
  {
    q: "Is there a psychologist job in the armed forces?",
    a: "Yes, through DRDO's Recruitment and Assessment Centre. In its 2022 advertisement, 17 of the 20 Psychology Scientist 'B' vacancies were for the Indian Armed Services selection boards and 3 were for DRDO. The posts are not advertised every year, so watch rac.gov.in."
  },
  {
    q: "Can a government psychologist run a private practice?",
    a: "It depends on the employer, the post and its service rules. Ask for the rule in writing before you plan around it. If outside work is allowed, an RCI-registered clinical psychologist can add a practice or online counselling beside the post."
  },
  {
    q: "Will AI replace government psychologists?",
    a: "Not the regulated clinical post in the near term. Assessment, therapy and the signed report need a registered, accountable person. AI can help with drafting and summaries, but never paste patient details into a public AI tool, and follow your hospital's data rules."
  }
];

const faqJsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  mainEntity: faqItems.map((item) => ({
    "@type": "Question",
    name: item.q,
    acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: item.a },
  })),
};
---

<BlogPostLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical={canonical}
  category="government-jobs"
  publishedAt={publishedDateISO}
  publishedLabel={publishedDateLabel}
  authorName={authorName}
  authorUrl={authorUrl}
  authorRole={authorRole}
  jsonLdExtras={[faqJsonLd]}
>
  <p class="lead-para">
    Government psychologist salary in India per month runs from about Rs 25,000 on entry-level contract posts to about Rs 91,000 at the first step of a Level 10 central post, counting basic pay plus dearness allowance. The gap depends first on one thing: whether the post sits on a government pay scale or is a fixed-pay contract.
  </p>

  <div class="key-takeaways">
    <p class="key-takeaways__label">The short version</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Short answer:</strong> In the notices checked (2022 to 2026), contract clinical psychologist posts paid Rs 25,000 to Rs 50,000 a month. Level 10 posts, such as DRDO and armed forces selection boards or AIIMS-type hospitals, start at Rs 56,100 basic pay.</li>
      <li><strong>How to judge any notice:</strong> "Pay level plus DA" means a government pay scale. "Consolidated" means one fixed amount. Clinical posts also ask for an RCI-recognised clinical course and registration.</li>
      <li><strong>Growth:</strong> The pay scale is fixed, so the high-income skill portfolio you build beside the post decides how fast you move toward earlier financial freedom.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <p>
    Three things set the monthly figure: the pay level or fixed amount in the notice, whether dearness allowance (DA) and house rent allowance (HRA) are added on top, and whether the post is regular or on contract.
  </p>

  <p>
    Figures come from official recruitment notices and a pay-level calculation, checked on 15 November 2026. Pay varies by city, employer and skill, and each notice has its own terms.
  </p>

  <p class="more-guides">If you are weighing a government post against other routes, <a href="/services/career-counselling-and-career-guidance/career-counselling-for-government-jobs/">career counselling for government jobs</a> is the direct route, and more <a href="/blog/government-jobs/">Government Jobs guides</a> sit in the same section.</p>

  <nav class="jump-nav" aria-label="Article sections">
    <p class="jump-nav__label">Jump to section</p>
    <ul class="jump-nav__list">
      <li><a href="#pay">Pay, post by post</a></li>
      <li><a href="#math">Level 10 to monthly pay</a></li>
      <li><a href="#type">Regular or contract</a></li>
      <li><a href="#qualify">Qualification and registration</a></li>
      <li><a href="#routes">Routes, strongest growth first</a></li>
      <li><a href="#reality">Ceiling, growth and AI</a></li>
      <li><a href="#who-pays">Who pays you</a></li>
      <li><a href="#money">Money check</a></li>
      <li><a href="#checkpoint">The four questions</a></li>
      <li><a href="#gate3">The three proofs</a></li>
      <li><a href="#mistakes">Expensive mistakes</a></li>
      <li><a href="#next-step">What to do next</a></li>
      <li><a href="#sources">Where the figures come from</a></li>
      <li><a href="#faq">FAQs</a></li>
    </ul>
  </nav>

  <h2 id="pay">Government psychologist salary per month, post by post</h2>
  <p>
    Each row is one real notice. Read the latest notice before you plan around any number.
  </p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table paths-table--wide">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Post and notice</th>
          <th>Monthly pay in the notice</th>
          <th>Type</th>
          <th>What it asked for</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Post and notice"><strong>Psychology Scientist 'B'</strong>, DRDO and armed forces selection boards (RAC advertisement 141, 2022)</td>
          <td data-label="Monthly pay in the notice">Level 10, basic Rs 56,100. About Rs 88,000 a month with HRA and allowances at metro rates, as quoted then</td>
          <td data-label="Type">Regular, Group A</td>
          <td data-label="What it asked for">First Class master's in Psychology, plus a valid GATE (XH) score or UGC NET for Assistant Professor</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Post and notice"><strong>Child psychologist</strong>, AIIMS Bathinda (2025)</td>
          <td data-label="Monthly pay in the notice">Level 10, basic Rs 56,100 plus DA</td>
          <td data-label="Type">Contract, 179 days at first, up to two years</td>
          <td data-label="What it asked for">MA or MSc Psychology, M.Phil in Clinical Psychology and 2 years in child and adolescent mental health</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Post and notice"><strong>Clinical Psychologist</strong>, Health Services, Kerala PSC (category 428/2025)</td>
          <td data-label="Monthly pay in the notice">Pay scale Rs 55,200 to Rs 1,15,300</td>
          <td data-label="Type">Direct recruitment</td>
          <td data-label="What it asked for">M.Phil in Clinical Psychology or a two-year equivalent from an RCI-approved institute, plus RCI registration</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Post and notice"><strong>Clinical Psychologist</strong>, Tele MANAS, Delhi State Health Society (2024)</td>
          <td data-label="Monthly pay in the notice">Rs 50,000. The counsellor post paid Rs 35,000</td>
          <td data-label="Type">Annual contract</td>
          <td data-label="What it asked for">M.Phil in Clinical Psychology preferred. An MA or MSc in Psychology was also listed</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Post and notice"><strong>Clinical Psychologist</strong>, NIMHANS brain health project (2024)</td>
          <td data-label="Monthly pay in the notice">Rs 40,000 consolidated</td>
          <td data-label="Type">Project contract</td>
          <td data-label="What it asked for">M.Phil in Clinical Psychology, or an MA or MSc in Psychology if none was available</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Post and notice"><strong>Clinical Psychologist</strong>, NHM Karnataka mental health staff (September 2026, a job-listing site's summary)</td>
          <td data-label="Monthly pay in the notice">Rs 25,000</td>
          <td data-label="Type">Contract</td>
          <td data-label="What it asked for">A regular-course degree in psychology, not by correspondence. Confirm on the official notice</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Post and notice"><strong>Assistant Professor or Senior Consultant, Clinical Psychology</strong>, NIMHANS Tele MANAS centre (2024)</td>
          <td data-label="Monthly pay in the notice">Rs 1,30,000 consolidated. The lower post paid Rs 1,05,000</td>
          <td data-label="Type">Project contract</td>
          <td data-label="What it asked for">M.Phil and PhD in Clinical Psychology, plus 3 years of teaching or research after the PhD</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="note-line">
    "Consolidated" usually means one fixed amount with no separate DA or HRA. Level 10 posts add DA and HRA on top of basic pay.
  </p>

  <h2 id="math">How a Level 10 pay level becomes a monthly figure</h2>
  <p>
    Level 10 starts at Rs 56,100 basic pay in the 7th Pay Commission matrix. The Union Cabinet raised central DA from 60% to 63% of basic pay from 1 July 2026, announced on 28 October 2026.
  </p>
  <div class="ladder">
    <div class="ladder-step">
      <div class="ladder-step__num">01</div>
      <div>
        <div class="ladder-step__title">Basic pay: Rs 56,100</div>
        <p>The first step of Level 10, as written in the DRDO and AIIMS notices.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="ladder-step">
      <div class="ladder-step__num">02</div>
      <div>
        <div class="ladder-step__title">DA at 63%: Rs 35,343</div>
        <p>DA is a share of basic pay, and the government revises it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="ladder-step">
      <div class="ladder-step__num">03</div>
      <div>
        <div class="ladder-step__title">Basic plus DA: Rs 91,443</div>
        <p>Pay before HRA, allowances and deductions at the first step of Level 10.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="ladder-step">
      <div class="ladder-step__num">04</div>
      <div>
        <div class="ladder-step__title">Then add and subtract</div>
        <p>HRA and transport allowance depend on the city. Pension contribution, tax and other deductions come off.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p>
    That is worked arithmetic from the published pay level and DA rate, not a pay slip. The 2022 DRDO advertisement quoted about Rs 88,000 a month with HRA at metro rates, when DA was lower.
  </p>
  <p>
    Pay levels can change when a new pay commission is implemented, so read any figure as today's picture, not a promise.
  </p>

  <h2 id="type">Regular post or contract post: what changes in your monthly pay</h2>
  <div class="split-grid">
    <div class="split-card split-card--grow">
      <div class="split-card__label">Regular post</div>
      <ul>
        <li>Pay comes from a pay level or pay scale, with DA and HRA added.</li>
        <li>Selection is by test and interview. The DRDO round used a subject exam first, then an interview, weighted 80 to 20.</li>
        <li>Postings can be anywhere. The armed forces psychology posts carried a liability to serve anywhere in India, including remote and field areas.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="split-card split-card--risk">
      <div class="split-card__label">Contract or project post</div>
      <ul>
        <li>Pay is one fixed amount, or basic plus DA at some AIIMS campuses.</li>
        <li>The term is short. AIIMS Bathinda ran 179 days at first, up to two years or until a regular appointment. Delhi's Tele MANAS posts renewed each year after review.</li>
        <li>Most contract notices do not promise a regular post. Plan your next step before the term ends.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 id="qualify">Qualification and registration behind each post</h2>
  <p>
    The pay line is only half of a notice. The other half decides whether you can apply at all.
  </p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Gate</th>
          <th>What it means</th>
          <th>Where it appeared</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Gate"><strong>Master's in Psychology</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What it means">The base degree. DRDO asked for First Class</td>
          <td data-label="Where it appeared">Every post above</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Gate"><strong>RCI-recognised clinical course</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What it means">M.Phil in Clinical Psychology, or the two-year equivalent that is replacing it</td>
          <td data-label="Where it appeared">AIIMS, Kerala PSC, NIMHANS and Delhi notices</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Gate"><strong>RCI registration</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What it means">Enrolment on the Rehabilitation Council of India register as a clinical psychologist</td>
          <td data-label="Where it appeared">Kerala PSC notice</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Gate"><strong>GATE (XH) or UGC NET</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What it means">A national test score, used before the subject exam</td>
          <td data-label="Where it appeared">DRDO Psychology Scientist 'B'</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Gate"><strong>PhD plus experience</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What it means">Research or teaching years after the doctorate</td>
          <td data-label="Where it appeared">NIMHANS faculty-level posts</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    Under the Mental Healthcare Act 2017, the clinical psychologist title needs a recognised clinical qualification. A general MA or MSc in psychology does not give it by itself.
  </p>
  <p>
    The RCI notice kept the M.Phil running for the 2024-25 and 2025-26 sessions, and reports say it is moving to a two-year master's-level course. Check the RCI website for the rule that applies to your intake year.
  </p>
  <div class="honest-take">
    <p class="honest-take__label">Honest take</p>
    <p>
      You face two filters, not one. First a course seat: a 2025 listing for the NIMHANS M.Phil showed 32 seats in total, 23 of them all-India. Then a post: the 2022 DRDO round had 20 psychology vacancies for the whole country, and the Kerala notice above had one.
    </p>
    <p>
      We give no selection odds. Count the posts in the last few notices before you plan a whole year around one.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="routes">Routes for a psychologist who wants government pay, strongest growth first</h2>
  <p>
    These are rated for how far your own effort can grow income beyond a pay scale. The ratings are judgement, not statistics.
  </p>
  <div class="route-grid">
    <div class="route-card">
      <div class="route-card__top">
        <span class="route-card__n">01</span>
        <span class="chip chip--high">Scalable</span>
      </div>
      <h3>Training, workshops and assessment services for schools, colleges and companies</h3>
      <p class="route-card__why">A repeatable programme can reach many groups, so income is not limited to your own session hours.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>Who pays you</span>Schools, colleges, employers and NGOs.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--violet"><span>What earns trust</span>Your degree, a clear outline and feedback from the first group.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--gold"><span>Watch out</span>Stay inside your qualification. Clinical work needs RCI registration.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>How it grows</span>Turn one workshop into a fixed package and add a trainer.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="route-card">
      <div class="route-card__top">
        <span class="route-card__n">02</span>
        <span class="chip chip--mid">Scalable with a business layer</span>
      </div>
      <h3>Private practice or online counselling after RCI registration</h3>
      <p class="route-card__why">You set the fee and the schedule, and can add group programmes and supervision later.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>Who pays you</span>Clients and families.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--violet"><span>What earns trust</span>Registration, supervised experience and referrals from doctors and schools.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--gold"><span>Watch out</span>The first clients come slowly. A government post may restrict outside work.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>How it grows</span>Group programmes, supervision of juniors and institute contracts.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="route-card">
      <div class="route-card__top">
        <span class="route-card__n">03</span>
        <span class="chip chip--low">Not so scalable</span>
      </div>
      <h3>Regular central post: DRDO and armed forces selection boards, and Level 10 hospital posts</h3>
      <p class="route-card__why">Stable pay and DA, but a fixed ladder and very few posts.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>Who pays you</span>The government, through the pay matrix.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--violet"><span>What earns trust</span>Marks, GATE or NET, an interview and the exact qualification asked.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--gold"><span>Watch out</span>Postings can be remote, and notices are irregular.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>How it grows</span>Promotions by service rules, then a practice or training work after service.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="route-card">
      <div class="route-card__top">
        <span class="route-card__n">04</span>
        <span class="chip chip--low">Not so scalable</span>
      </div>
      <h3>State health service post through a public service commission</h3>
      <p class="route-card__why">A pay scale and a state job, with one or a few vacancies per notice.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>Who pays you</span>The state government.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--violet"><span>What earns trust</span>The RCI-recognised course, RCI registration and the exam rank.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--gold"><span>Watch out</span>Notices are rare, and some are reserved for set categories.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>How it grows</span>State promotion rules and posts in larger hospitals.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="route-card">
      <div class="route-card__top">
        <span class="route-card__n">05</span>
        <span class="chip chip--low">Not so scalable</span>
      </div>
      <h3>Contract posts under health missions and projects</h3>
      <p class="route-card__why">The easiest to enter, but pay is fixed and the term is short.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>Who pays you</span>A state health society, a mission or a funded project.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--violet"><span>What earns trust</span>The course asked for and a record of supervised cases.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--gold"><span>Watch out</span>Clinical psychologist pay in the notices checked ran from Rs 25,000 to Rs 50,000, with no promise of a regular post.</p>
      <p class="route-row route-row--teal"><span>How it grows</span>Use the term to build experience, then move to a pay-scale post or your own practice.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--teal">
    <p>
      <strong>The ownership path:</strong> an RCI-registered private practice or a training service scales because you set the price, can add programmes and juniors, and can reach people beyond one city. Check your employer's rule on outside work first.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="reality">Pay ceiling, growth and AI for a government psychologist</h2>
  <div class="honest-take">
    <p class="honest-take__label">Honest take</p>
    <p>
      Pay climbs by the pay matrix and promotion rules, not by how many people you help. The work is assessments, therapy, case records and reports, and on armed forces selection boards, testing candidates and accepting postings that can be remote.
    </p>
    <p>
      Salary alone can make financial independence slower. Saving and investing from a steady salary still build wealth.
    </p>
  </div>
  <p>
    AI helps most with paperwork: drafting a report from your own notes and summarising papers. Assessment, therapy and the signed report stay with a registered, accountable person, so the risk to regulated clinical posts is low for now.
  </p>
  <p>
    The pressure is on generic wellness chat and entry-level counselling that needs no registration. That is our read, not a statistic.
  </p>
  <p>
    Staged path: now, learn to use AI for drafts and summaries within your hospital's data rules, and never paste patient details into a public tool. Later, add the skills AI cannot replace: assessment judgement, supervision and clear explanation to families.
  </p>
  <p>
    Build a high-income skill portfolio beside the post: one core skill (clinical assessment), one multiplier (training design or data handling) and proof others can check. These are the decisions that unlock high income opportunities, whatever the pay scale says.
  </p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Better-fit option</th>
          <th>Why it can beat this one</th>
          <th>Catch</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Better-fit option"><strong>People analytics, HR or UX research with a psychology degree</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Why it can beat this one">No licence gate, and pay can grow with company size and results</td>
          <td data-label="Catch">Needs data or product skills, and the work is not clinical</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Better-fit option"><strong>Private practice after a few years in a hospital post</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Why it can beat this one">You own the fee, schedule and growth</td>
          <td data-label="Catch">Slow first years, and outside-work rules may apply</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    The pay and routes for these are in <a href="/blog/career-options/career-in-psychology-india-salary-scope/">career in psychology in India: salary and scope</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="who-pays">Who pays a government psychologist, and how they judge you</h2>
  <p>
    The payer is the government: a hospital, a state health society, a selection board or a funded project. Before paying, it checks the qualification written in the notice, RCI registration for clinical posts, a test score or exam rank, and the experience the notice names, such as two years in child and adolescent mental health.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first skill to build is careful assessment with clear written reports, backed by supervised cases. Selling matters mainly for the side route or the move after the post: say who you help, show one anonymised outcome, ask doctors and schools for referrals, and hold one honest conversation about your fee.
  </p>

  <h2 id="money">Money check before you pay for the course</h2>
  <p>
    Our strongest suggestion: keep a course or degree fee near a tenth of the family education budget, and treat spending above roughly a fifth as a caution that needs course-specific evidence. This does not apply to very cheap online courses. Free YouTube lessons and low-priced courses on sites like Udemy or Coursera need little budget care, and the same course through a university certificate can cost 30 to 100 times more.
  </p>
  <p>
    An illustration, not a real fee: on a Rs 5 lakh education budget, a tenth is Rs 50,000 for the main course and a fifth is Rs 1,00,000. Spend the rest on books, supervised practice, travel for interviews and a reserve for the months between contracts.
  </p>
  <p>
    Free lectures can help you test the subject and prepare for an entrance test. They do not replace an RCI-recognised clinical course, supervised training or registration. Check recognition on the RCI website before you pay any fee.
  </p>

  <h2 id="checkpoint">The four questions for a government psychologist post</h2>
  <p>
    Test the choice with <strong>Four questions to answer:</strong> does this work suit you, can your life carry it, are posts opening, and will AI take your part? If one line stays empty, wait before you pay for a course.
  </p>
  <div class="protocol">
    <div class="protocol-row">
      <div class="protocol-row__num">01</div>
      <div>
        <div class="protocol-row__title">Your fit: can you do this work every day?</div>
        <p>Case records, assessments and sitting with distress make up the job. Spend time with a practising clinical psychologist before you commit to a clinical course.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="protocol-row">
      <div class="protocol-row__num">02</div>
      <div>
        <div class="protocol-row__title">Your situation: can your family carry the runway?</div>
        <p>The route runs from a master's, to a clinical course, to a wait for a notice. Many first posts are contracts at Rs 25,000 to Rs 50,000, so plan the gap.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="protocol-row">
      <div class="protocol-row__num">03</div>
      <div>
        <div class="protocol-row__title">Job market: how many posts really open?</div>
        <p>Count the vacancies in the last few notices of your target employer. One to three posts per notice is common, and the 2022 DRDO round listed 20 for the country.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="protocol-row">
      <div class="protocol-row__num">04</div>
      <div>
        <div class="protocol-row__title">AI-proof: what stays yours?</div>
        <p>Assessment judgement, therapy and the signed report stay with you. Drafting and summaries can get AI help within data rules.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 id="gate3">Three proofs before you commit</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Three proofs to pass:</strong> show it, say it in 30 seconds to 2 minutes, and get it checked by people who would judge or hire.
  </p>
  <div class="gates-block">
    <div class="gates-row">
      <div class="gate">
        <span class="gate__num">Proof 1</span>
        <span class="gate__name">Show it</span>
        <p>Keep an anonymised practicum log and one assessment report written from a supervised case.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gate">
        <span class="gate__num">Proof 2</span>
        <span class="gate__name">Say it</span>
        <p>Explain one assessment result and its limits to a non-psychologist in 30 seconds to 2 minutes, as an interview board would ask.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gate">
        <span class="gate__num">Proof 3</span>
        <span class="gate__name">Get it checked</span>
        <p>Ask a supervising clinical psychologist, a psychiatrist and a senior colleague whether they would rely on your report.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 id="mistakes">Expensive mistakes with government psychologist pay</h2>
  <div class="mistake-list">
    <div class="mistake">
      <div class="mistake__num">01</div>
      <div>
        <div class="mistake__title">Comparing basic pay with another job's in-hand pay</div>
        <p>Basic pay is only the start. Add DA and HRA for a pay-scale post, then subtract deductions, before you compare it with a private offer.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mistake">
      <div class="mistake__num">02</div>
      <div>
        <div class="mistake__title">Reading a consolidated contract figure as a pay scale</div>
        <p>A contract of Rs 40,000 has no scale, no promised DA and a short term. Ask what happens when the term ends.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mistake">
      <div class="mistake__num">03</div>
      <div>
        <div class="mistake__title">Joining a clinical course without checking RCI recognition</div>
        <p>A course the RCI does not recognise can close the clinical posts. Check the RCI list and the rule for your intake year first.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mistake">
      <div class="mistake__num">04</div>
      <div>
        <div class="mistake__title">Waiting for one notice with nothing else running</div>
        <p>Notices are irregular. Keep a paid counselling or training job going, so a missed notice does not stop your income and your proof. GATE (XH) or NET preparation also keeps teaching and research doors open.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mistake">
      <div class="mistake__num">05</div>
      <div>
        <div class="mistake__title">Paying anyone for a post</div>
        <p>Apply only on the official website. No real government job asks for money.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 id="next-step">What to do next</h2>
  <p>
    Pick one post type from the table, read its latest notice end to end, and write down the pay line, the qualification and the number of posts. Then list the proof you can build beside it.
  </p>
  <p>
    A specialist can look at your strengths, finances and goals with you. A sensible first step is <a href="/services/career-counselling-and-career-guidance/career-counselling-for-government-jobs/">career counselling for government jobs</a>. The aim is a high-income skill portfolio and the decisions that unlock high income opportunities, on an earlier path to financial freedom.
  </p>
  <p>
    Read also <a href="/blog/government-jobs/state-vs-central-government-jobs-india/">state vs central government jobs</a>, <a href="/blog/skills/skills-required-for-psychology-careers-india/">skills required for psychology careers</a> and <a href="/blog/government-jobs/government-exam-preparation-while-working-india/">government exam preparation while working</a>.
  </p>
  <p class="note-line">
    Recruitment details change, so use only the official recruitment website of each employer.
  </p>

